# CLOSURE (qa-pr1196-r1, quality-mgr): PR #1196 at d9ef17ca3 adds
# crates/atm-http-runtime/src/doctor_observability.rs::project_counter_health
# which populates a structured report.observability field (jsonl{forwarded_total,
# dropped_queue_full_total,dropped_reentrant_total}, timeline{written_total,
# dropped_queue_full_total,dropped_persist_error_total}, degraded: Vec<String>)
# identical in shape to /v1/health's RetainedObservabilityHealthResponse
# (crates/atm-core/src/observability_counters.rs:26-51), wired into the real
# doctor dispatch path at storage_and_nudge_router.rs:566. New test
# doctor_observability_fields_match_health_projection
# (storage_and_nudge_router.rs:2203) drives the real dispatch() path and
# asserts field-for-field parity. Independently confirmed by quality-mgr,
# req-qa, and rust-qa-agent (566+92+200 tests green, 0 clippy warnings).
# `cargo test -p atm-http-runtime doctor_observability_fields_match_health_projection`:
# 1 passed. This closes the structural gap this finding was filed for.

